WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.590
Film Courage:&nbsp; Jeff, you recently wrote a
book and I was wondering if you could tell

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.640
me the title of it first?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.980
Jeff Leisawitz:&nbsp; Not ***ing Around: The No
***hit Guide For Getting Your Creative Dreams

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.980
Off The Ground.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.980
Film Courage:&nbsp; Okay.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.219
I like the title.&nbsp;

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:14.219
But why the title?&nbsp;

00:00:14.219 --> 00:00:15.509
Jeff Leisawitz: Why the title?&nbsp;

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:19.860
Well it’s straight to the point and it pretty
much says what the book is about in one line.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.470
Film Courage:&nbsp; So where were you when you
decided to come up with the idea and was there

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.960
something in your life that triggered this
in you where you said “You know what?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.260
Jeff this is no more NFA.”

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.000
Which I know is your catchphrase and is really
cool, anybody who hears it knows okay, it’s

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.740
a kick in the ***.&nbsp; It means let’s get
going.&nbsp;

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.740
But did this happen to you?&nbsp;

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.950
Did something happen?

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:47.620
Jeff Leisawitz: Well, I have always (generally)
been NFA my whole life without knowing it

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.140
was called that.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.140
&nbsp;

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.739
I’ve always been pretty motivated and ambitious
to do things, mostly creative things and business

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:56.809
ideas.&nbsp;

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:03.390
Even as a kid I got into music and played
in lots of bands and got a four track and

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.390
that kind of stuff.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.860
I wanted to move to LA and become a rock star.&nbsp;

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:13.240
I did move to LA but I didn’t quite become
a rock star, but that’s okay.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.140
But this book happened sort of by accident.&nbsp;

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:22.270
I had a free Saturday or Sunday morning one
day and I coffeed-up at a local Seattle coffee

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:27.070
shop and I just started writing as I often
do.&nbsp;

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.409
I wrote one of the chapters in the book.&nbsp;

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:37.450
When I was done I was like “You know, this
would be a good idea for a book for just empowering

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.450
creatives.”

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:44.820
And what I realized after I wrote the book
was that everything (well, not everything)

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.230
but many things in my life were actually leading
up to this book.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.320
So for instance I have been a creative person
my whole life.&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.220
A musician, a filmmaker, a writer, photographer,
etc.&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.440
But I’ve also been into empowering people
my whole life.&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.720
I was a music journalist when I was empowering
other musicians.&nbsp;

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:10.520
I’m a teacher of songwriting at a college
up near Tacoma, near Seattle.&nbsp;

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:15.870
I’m a life coach.&nbsp;

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:23.370
I practice something called NLP (Neuro-linguistic
re-patterning) which is talk therapy or counseling

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:29.689
to help people untangle the subconscious blocks
that keep them down in various different ways.

00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:30.689
&nbsp;

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:34.379
So after I wrote this book I kind of thought
about and was like “You know what?&nbsp;

00:02:34.379 --> 00:02:37.030
This is actually my mission.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.260
It’s like being creative and empowering.”

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.540
But I didn’t know that until I wrote the
book.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.180
If that makes any sense?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.490
Film Courage:&nbsp; It does.&nbsp;

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.410
Did you share the idea for the book with anyone?&nbsp;

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.880
Jeff Leisawitz:&nbsp; Sure.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:58.410
Initially, a friend of mine Steve we came
up with the term NFA probably a couple of

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.790
years before I wrote the book.&nbsp;

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.780
But we come up with lots of weird words and
terms.&nbsp;

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.930
And then this one just resurfaced so it seemed
like a good idea for a title.

